From c385e1b625fa27c17f42580e813f7708f703b998 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Londa <londa@fmcc>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:07:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: confirmBeforeChaseGuard - let an already-touched setup
 confirm first (default OFF)

Frequency diagnosis: 70% of armed setups die 'target reached before a confirmed entry',
100% after touching the zone. For a setup that touched the FVG on a PRIOR candle, attempt
confirm() BEFORE the chase guard: if an entry model fires on the target-take candle, the
entry existed and should not lose the same-candle race. Touch-this-candle stays behind the
guard (intrabar-ambiguous, fail safe). Default OFF; suite 1174 -> 1178.

HONEST RESULT on the requested window (2022-03-07..21):
  before fix: 0 closed trades
  after fix:  0 closed trades (unchanged)

diag_chase_split with the flag on shows why: 11 setups still die do-not-chase, all
after-touch, none recovered. On the target-take candle NO entry model confirms, so
confirm() returns False and the guard correctly still fires. The fix only helps when a
confirmation is actually AVAILABLE on that candle (e.g. some summer-2024 cases); here it
is not.

So this window's bottleneck is deeper than guard ordering: price reaches the FVG but
never produces a valid M15_CLOSE/LTF/no-wick entry before running to target. That is
entry-model sensitivity, not the timing race. The fix is correct and safe but does not
unblock every window. Next: measure how often a confirmation is available at all in the
touch->target window, and whether entry-model/confirmationWindowBars need adjustment.

No behaviour change (default OFF); spec restored byte-for-byte.
